From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:53:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] signal: a declined host fault marks the Play's end

PLA-847, for the game page's memory-kill note. iOS ends a process past
its memory limit with SIGKILL, which nothing can see, so the app takes
a Play whose process ended near the limit for a memory kill unless the
process marked another end first (app/Sources/WineHost/play_end.c). A
host crash during a Play comes here: a fault the runtime does not adopt
as the guest's (ml481's rule: a thread with no TEB, or host code's PC)
is declined, the default disposition is restored and the repeated fault
or abort() ends the process, by SIGSEGV, SIGBUS, SIGILL, SIGTRAP or
SIGABRT.

madeira_set_play_end_hook takes the host's hook before __wine_main;
ios_decline_foreign_fault calls it with the signal before restoring the
default disposition. The hook only opens, writes and closes a file it
named before the Play, so it may run in a signal handler. With no hook
nothing changes.

Linear: PLA-847
Class: host-app
Evidence: app/tests/play_end_test.c (the mark the hook writes; host checks; phone gates not run)
Offered-upstream: no; the hook serves the iOS app's own record of a Play
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 38a15cf..6b9aeba 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -10013,10 +10013,23 @@ static int ios_fault_is_foreign( const void *pc, const void *addr )
     return 1;
 }
 
+/* PLA-847: the host's end mark (app/Sources/WineHost/play_end.c), set before
+ * __wine_main. A declined fault is fatal: the default disposition ends the
+ * process when the fault repeats. iOS's memory kill is a SIGKILL nothing sees,
+ * so a Play whose process ended with no mark may have been ended for memory,
+ * and one marked here was not. The hook only opens, writes and closes a file. */
+static void (*ios_play_end_hook)( int sig );
+
+void madeira_set_play_end_hook( void (*hook)( int sig ) )
+{
+    ios_play_end_hook = hook;
+}
+
 /* Decline a foreign fault: report it with write(2)-only logging (the
  * interrupted thread may hold the malloc lock, so NOTHING here may allocate or
- * hit an unbound lazy stub), then restore the default disposition so the OS
- * reports honestly instead of us spinning forever inside our own handler. */
+ * hit an unbound lazy stub), mark the Play's end, then restore the default
+ * disposition so the OS reports honestly instead of us spinning forever inside
+ * our own handler. */
 static void ios_decline_foreign_fault( int sig, const void *pc, const void *addr )
 {
     static int declined_n;
@@ -10026,6 +10039,7 @@ static void ios_decline_foreign_fault( int sig, const void *pc, const void *addr
         dprintf( 2, "[host-fault] sig=%d pc=%p addr=%p on a NON-guest thread — declining to adopt "
                     "(would have deadlocked in our own handler) rev=ml481\n", sig, pc, addr );
     }
+    if (ios_play_end_hook) ios_play_end_hook( sig );
     signal( sig, SIG_DFL );
 }
 #endif
